question:
What does this lambda return?
Func<int, int> square = x => x * x;
Console.WriteLine(square(5));

What does this multi-line lambda do?
Func<int, int> compute = x => {
  int result = x * 2;
  return result;
};
Console.WriteLine(compute(10));

What does this lambda with multiple parameters do?
Func<int, int, int> add = (a, b) => a + b;
Console.WriteLine(add(3, 4));

What is captured by this lambda?
int x = 10;
Func<int, int> add = y => x + y;
Console.WriteLine(add(5));

What is the output when captured variable changes?
int x = 5;
Func<int> get = () => x;
x = 10;
Console.WriteLine(get());

What does this Action lambda do?
Action<string> greet = name => Console.WriteLine($"Hello {name}");
greet("Alice");

What does this lambda without parameters do?
Func<int> random = () => new Random().Next(10);
var x = random();
Console.WriteLine(x < 10);

What is the output of this loop with lambda?
var funcs = new List<Func<int>>();
for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
  funcs.Add(() => i);
}
Console.WriteLine(funcs[0]());

What does this delegate expression do?
Predicate<int> isEven = x => x % 2 == 0;
Console.WriteLine(isEven(4));

What does this comparison lambda do?
Comparison<int> compare = (a, b) => a - b;
Console.WriteLine(compare(5, 3));
